1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:06,176
Minister Kerbu: Today Kivona signs with SunRiver Power. One hundred megawatts of light for our people!

2
00:00:07,226 --> 00:00:09,125
Emson Anahct: We are ready to build, Minister.

3
00:00:10,175 --> 00:00:13,994
Tidianie Eugom: An MoU is a good start, Emson. It is not financing.

4
00:00:15,444 --> 00:00:17,108
Everything looks promising.

5
00:00:19,058 --> 00:00:21,277
But is the project really ready?

6
00:00:24,427 --> 00:00:26,368
Bankable is not enough.

7
00:00:29,918 --> 00:00:32,265
Test one. Can the utility pay?

8
00:00:34,865 --> 00:00:39,793
For every one hundred billed, seventy are collected. Ninety-five are needed.

9
00:00:41,293 --> 00:00:43,277
Belpau: So if we miss a payment to SunRiver...

10
00:00:43,577 --> 00:00:47,524
Paul Ahmak: ...the State guarantee is called, and the bill goes to the Treasury.

11
00:00:49,274 --> 00:00:51,877
Test two. Can the grid absorb the power?

12
00:00:54,477 --> 00:01:01,154
A one hundred megawatt plant. A grid that can absorb sixty. Forty megawatts: paid, never used.

13
00:01:02,904 --> 00:01:05,208
Test three. Who carries the risk?

14
00:01:08,058 --> 00:01:10,341
The tariff: ten US cents.

15
00:01:12,491 --> 00:01:14,987
Year one: sixty Kivona francs.

16
00:01:17,137 --> 00:01:18,886
Year five: eighty.

17
00:01:20,836 --> 00:01:24,313
Same dollar tariff. One third more in local money.

18
00:01:26,763 --> 00:01:28,747
Who carries the currency risk?

19
00:01:32,197 --> 00:01:35,056
Test four. Can the public sector live with it?

20
00:01:37,206 --> 00:01:38,507
Tidianie Eugom: Our loan is protected.

21
00:01:39,557 --> 00:01:40,944
Enilec Mok: Protected by whom?

22
00:01:41,994 --> 00:01:43,231
Tidianie Eugom: Well... by you.

23
00:01:44,681 --> 00:01:47,646
Enilec Mok: A guarantee needs almost no cash on the day we sign.

24
00:01:49,596 --> 00:01:51,921
Enilec Mok: That is exactly why it is dangerous.

25
00:01:54,671 --> 00:01:57,359
Red team. What could make this deal fail?

26
00:01:58,159 --> 00:02:00,122
The offtaker cannot pay.

27
00:02:00,672 --> 00:02:02,954
The grid cannot absorb the power.

28
00:02:03,504 --> 00:02:06,342
The government carries hidden obligations.

29
00:02:06,892 --> 00:02:11,094
Don't ask whether the project is attractive. Ask what could break it.

30
00:02:14,244 --> 00:02:15,417
Should we sign?

31
00:02:17,967 --> 00:02:18,906
Bankable.

32
00:02:19,506 --> 00:02:20,508
Affordable.

33
00:02:21,108 --> 00:02:22,367
Executable.

34
00:02:22,967 --> 00:02:24,098
Sustainable.

35
00:02:24,698 --> 00:02:27,492
Bankable is not the same as sustainable.

36
00:02:31,492 --> 00:02:34,265
Belpau: Bankable is the start. Sustainable is the goal.

37
00:02:35,715 --> 00:02:37,656
Bankable is not enough.

38
00:02:38,556 --> 00:02:40,754
Before you sign, test the deal.
